  (text "As delivered: every channel pull-up (topology jumper 1-2); FUEL 100R (the factory 0-30R sender), ETEMP 1k, OILP 220R, AMB 100k bridged.\nPull-up mode: any resistive sender whose other end is ground (the block, the tank, or its return pin). Pull-down mode: a sender fed from the channel's V pin, or a 3-wire 0.5-4.5 V transducer (OILP 100k as a light load; or no value bridged).\nThe pull-ups come straight from +5 V, not through the PTCs (their drop would read as level error). Sender selection: SensorCard/DATASHEET.md." (at 220 244.88 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left top)) (uuid "36707b4a-0ca1-5344-8c77-cb17d19a80db"))
